            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meta-ibm/recipes-phosphor/fans/phosphor-fan_%.bbappend",
                    "line": 46,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "The recipe was installing this service into both the multi-user.target and the obmc-chassis-poweron@.target instances. To get SYSTEMD_SERVICE to support installing in both, it would seem we need the service file to indicate both in the \n\n[Install] directive?  Unfortunately due to the lack of systemd/yocto support in the past for the Install section, we've been commenting them out and relying on the recipe logic to install where it made sense. This new change is implying to me we need to go back to all of the service files and ensure their Install section is correct to move over to just using SYSTEMD_SERVICE?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-ibm/recipes-phosphor/fans/phosphor-fan_%.bbappend",
                    "line": 46,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "> The recipe was installing this service into both the multi-user.target and the obmc-chassis-poweron@.target instances.\n\nThanks for reviewing and catching that.  That's a mistake.\n\nI found a more tactical solution for these two recipes that I'll put up as a separate commit while we figure out what to do next.\n\n> To get SYSTEMD_SERVICE to support installing in both, it would seem we need the service file to indicate both in the [Install] directive? Unfortunately due to the lack of systemd/yocto support in the past for the Install section, we've been commenting them out and relying on the recipe logic to install where it made sense. This new change is implying to me we need to go back to all of the service files and ensure their Install section is correct to move over to just using SYSTEMD_SERVICE?\n\nThere _seems_ to be more support now for automatic installation but I'm not 100% convinced it works without doing some more experimentation.  It definitely works for all service that are installed into multi-user.target (even if they are templates), but I don't know if it properly handles all the `[Install]` directives.\n\nMore experimentation required."
                }
            ],
